\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Thee will I love, my strength, my tower,
\par Thee will I love, my joy, my crown,
\par Thee will I love with all my power,
\par In all Thy works, and Thee alone;
\par Thee will I love, till the pure fire
\par Fill my whole soul with chaste desire.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Ah, why did I so late Thee know,
\par Thee, lovelier than the sons of men!
\par Ah, why did I no sooner go
\par To Thee, the only ease in pain!
\par Ashamed, I sigh, and inly mourn,
\par That I so late to Thee did turn.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. In darkness willingly I strayed,
\par I sought Thee, yet from Thee I roved,
\par Far wide my wandering thoughts were spread,
\par Thy creatures more than Thee I loved;
\par And now if more at length I see,
\par 'Tis through Thy light, and comes from Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. I thank Thee, uncreated Sun,
\par That Thy bright beams on me have shined;
\par I thank Thee, who hast overthrown
\par My foes, and healed my wounded mind;
\par I thank Thee, whose enlivening voice
\par Bids my freed heart in Thee rejoice.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Give to mine eyes refreshing tears,
\par Give to my heart chaste, hallowed fires,
\par Give to my soul, with filial fears,
\par The love that all heaven's host inspires;
\par That all my powers, with all their might,
\par In Thy sole glory may unite.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Thee will I love, my joy, my crown,
\par Thee will I love, my Lord, my God;
\par Thee will I love, beneath Thy frown,
\par Or smile, Thy sceptre, or Thy rod;
\par What though my flesh and heart decay?
\par Thee shall I love in endless day!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

